# Line endings are the repository's business, not each clone's.
#
# Everything already stored here uses LF, because every machine that has
# committed to it happened to have core.autocrlf=true. That is a per-clone
# setting: a contributor without it would commit CRLF and every line of the
# file would show as changed. This makes the normalisation a property of the
# repository instead, so the stored form is LF regardless of who clones it and
# Windows working copies still get CRLF on checkout.
* text=auto

# The binaries are marked rather than left to detection. text=auto decides by
# looking for NUL bytes and would classify all of these correctly, but
# inpoutx64.sys is a kernel driver and inpoutx64.dll the only path this
# project has to the hardware: a misclassification would rewrite bytes inside
# them, and the cost of being explicit is three lines.
*.dll binary
*.sys binary
*.ico binary
*.png binary

# Not an image or a driver, but not text either: a 2 MB NVRAM capture whose
# exact bytes are the point of keeping it.
nvram.txt binary
